I downloaded and installed a binary distribution of xemacs on an Alpha
box with DU4.0d

Whenever I start xemacs I get the following error message:

canoepolo.pd.uwa.edu.au> /usr/local/bin/alpha-dec-osf3.2/xemacs 

WARNING:
couldn't find an obvious default for load-path, doc-directory, and
data-directory, and there were no defaults specified in paths.h when
XEmacs
was built.  Perhaps some directories don't exist, or the XEmacs
executable,
/usr/local/bin/alpha-dec-osf3.2/xemacs is in a strange place?

Without both exec-directory and load-path, XEmacs will be very broken.
Consider making a symbolic link from
/home/stuart/lib/xemacs-20.4/alpha-dec-osf3.2 to wherever the
appropriate
XEmacs exec-directory directory is, and from
/home/stuart/lib/xemacs-20.4/etc to wherever the appropriate XEmacs
data-directory is, and from /home/stuart/lib/xemacs-20.4/lisp to
wherever
the appropriate XEmacs lisp library is.
Warning: Cannot allocate colormap entry for "#D100C0EFAE93"


None of the menus or buttons work correctly.  What is wrong?

Thanks

Stu.


-- 
<------------------------------------------------------------------------------>
        
        Stuart Midgley
        Department of Physics, University of Western Australia

        stuart@physics.uwa.edu.au



