Stuart Midgley <stuart@physics.uwa.edu.au> writes:

> I downloaded and installed a binary distribution of xemacs on an Alpha
> box with DU4.0d
> 
> Whenever I start xemacs I get the following error message:
> 
> canoepolo.pd.uwa.edu.au> /usr/local/bin/alpha-dec-osf3.2/xemacs 

That's because XEmacs is looking for the directory names with `4.0'
instead of `3.2' in them.

Go to where you installed XEmacs, and make a symlinks from 4.0
to 3.2 directories.  For example:

        cd /usr/local/xemacs-20.4     # Where I installed it.
        cd lib/xemacs-20.4
        ln -s ./alpha-dec-osf3.2 alpha-dec-osf4.0
        cd ../../bin
        ln -s ./alpha-dec-osf3.2 alpha-dec-osf4.0

