In article <3557555F.E6C2C20F@cs.ou.edu>, Sirirut Vanichayobon
<svanicha@cs.ou.edu> wrote:
>I installed ADVFS on DU 4.0D.
>The daemon seems to be working and the GUI is also working, but
>when I try to create a new domain with mkfdmn I get the following error:
>
>mkfdmn: domain init error E_ADVFS_NOT_INSTALLED (-1108)
>mkfdmn: cannot create new domain "user_dmn".
>I used > mkfdmn /dev/rz5c user_dmn

Does your /sys/conf/<HOSTNAME> file have an entry for AdvFS

    options  MSFS

If it does not have this entry, then the kernel was not built with AdvFS
modules and as a result any attempt by utilities to access AdvFS features
will fail with the error E_ADVFS_NOT_INSTALLED.

So edit your /sys/conf/<HOSTNAME> file, then rebuild your kernel.

