On Tue, 12 May 1998 17:44:33 +0200, Nikola Milutinovic
<milutinn@EUnet.yu> wrote:

>Sirirut Vanichayobon wrote:
...
>> mkfdmn: domain init error E_ADVFS_NOT_INSTALLED (-1108)
>> mkfdmn: cannot create new domain "user_dmn".
>> I used > mkfdmn /dev/rz5c user_dmn
...

>Is there any chance that you really didn�t install all of AdvFS?
>Like, when installing, you didn�t choose AdvFS for either /[root] and
>/usr file systems and didn't install AdvFS subsets.

The error message says, that the ADVFS is not installed.
That is, most probably, the ADVFS driver itself has not been linked
into the kernel. 
Look if the "option MSFS" is in your config file. If not, put it in
and create a new kernel.
And, make sure your advfs license is active.

