Marc Kessler wrote:
> 
>    My executables compiled with f77 under DU 4.0B die with a
> /sbin/loader:  Fatal Error: set_program_attributes failed to set heap
> start
> 

Marc:
     The problem is that your process limits are lower than the
     "data + bss" size of the file you're tryint to load and execute. 
    
     If you do a "size" command on your file, you'll see the amount
     of heap it needs to be loaded.  Check that against your process
     limits and raise them accordingly.  

     If you're using the C-shell, the limit command is a place to
     start.  If you need to go further, raise the limits in 
     /etc/sysconfigtab.

Joe Mario
	

