We're having a bit of trouble with a large (51 MB) Digital UNIX v4.0b patch
 that we're trying to apply.  The patch has been running for an unusually
 long time now (over 7 1/2/ hours ... longer than it takes to do a full DU
operating system installation).  Is such a lengthy installation time
 "normal" for a DEC AlphaServer 2100 with two 300Mhz CPUs?

I've described our system's configuration and the weird problem we're
having below.   Any tips, clues, or suggestions would be greatly
appreciated !!!  :-)

Thanks

ERIC FERGUSON, Capt, USAF
Maxwell AFB AL

Phone:  334-953-5881 / DSN 493-5881
E-mail:  EFerguson@rco.maxwell.af.mil

===========================

We have two web servers, a Primary and a Backup ...

Primary:	DEC AlphaServer 2100 (with two 300MHz CPUs & SMP
Support enabled) .... OS is Digital UNIX v4.0b

Backup:	DECpc AXP 150 (single 150 MHz CPU) ... OS is also
Digital UNIX v4.0b

Patch we're trying to install:  duv40bas00006-19971216.tar (an
 aggregate patch, a little over 51 MB in size)

OUR PROBLEM:

We know how to install Digital UNIX patches (... have done several
 over the past few years).  We installed this particular patch on the
 Backup server first (the AXP 150) to ensure it worked correctly.
At the time of the install, we didn't note how long the patch actually
 took to install ... we started the patching process at the close of
business one afternoon (~ 4:30pm), and by the time we returned
to work the next morning (at 7:30am), it was finished (as expected).
  We let a couple of weeks go by before attempting the
 installation on the Primary server, so we could look for
 anything odd about the DU4's performance after the patch was applied.

Anyway, we tried to apply the same patch to our "big"
server (the AlphaServer 2100) last night ... you can see where
 this is going.  We thought, "hey, we'll just bring this puppy
down at 11:30pm, let the patch run (for a couple of hours or so),
 and we'll be finished and ready to go by 3:00am."  Well, it
 didn't happen that way ...

The installation process has been going non-stop since 11:30pm
 Central Time last night, and it's 7:30 am now as I write this
message.  My systems guy and I are thinking "Hey,
something is _not_ quite right, here!"

QUESTION:  Even though the patch is 51 MB in size, and
 though we _did_ select to install "all available patches" in
 the patch kit, should it take this long to install the patch?
  On a AlphaServer 2100 with two 300MHz CPUs?  At this
 point, it's been 8 hours, and it's _still_ going ... that's longer
 than it takes to install the operating system!

WEIRD THINGS WE NOTICED ABOUT THE INSTALL:

We followed the instructions that came with the patch kit
(as usual) to unpack the tar file.  We kicked off the install
using "dupatch" from single-user mode and did a
pre-installation check first.  The pre-installation check
